WEBVTT

00:03:02.115 --> 00:03:06.985
To the south of the continent of
Alecrast lies an island known as Lodoss.

00:03:07.053 --> 00:03:09.647
Said to have been created in
the fierce battle between...

00:03:09.722 --> 00:03:13.852
...Marfa, the Goddess of Creation and
Kardis, the Goddess of Destruction...

00:03:13.927 --> 00:03:17.557
...it is now known
as "The Accursed Island”.

00:03:22.101 --> 00:03:25.435
And now, in Lodoss, whose history
is painted with the hues of war...

00:03:25.505 --> 00:03:28.634
...new ambitions
have begun to stir.

00:03:29.943 --> 00:03:34.141
Why does a knight of Marmo
come to this far-flung place?

00:03:34.881 --> 00:03:39.512
What do you want here at the temple
of Marfa, the Goddess of the Earth?

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:43.353
Do you know the
origins of that sword?

00:03:43.423 --> 00:03:47.724
Its existence has caused nothing
but suffering for people.

00:03:48.027 --> 00:03:51.190
It was originally wielded
by the king of the demons.

00:03:51.264 --> 00:03:55.963
It should be sealed in the
deepest, darkest labyrinth there is.

00:03:56.035 --> 00:04:00.097
Forgive me, but I didn't
come here to listen to this.

00:04:01.541 --> 00:04:06.001
I have something to ask you...
Will you answer me truthfully?

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:09.039
| won't lie to you. However...

00:04:09.382 --> 00:04:14.445
Very well. I just ask that
you answer me honestly. Yes...

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:17.820
It has to do with the treasure
of the ice dragon, Bramd.

00:04:17.890 --> 00:04:19.221
Bramd's treasure?!

00:04:19.792 --> 00:04:24.229
I'm a vulgar man who wishes
to make his treasure mine!

00:04:25.865 --> 00:04:29.529
Long ago, the glorious Kingdom of
Sorcery entrusted the five ancient...

00:04:29.602 --> 00:04:32.867
...dragons with the Governor's
Treasures to guard for all eternity.

00:04:32.939 --> 00:04:36.671
However, the ice dragon
Bramd had no treasure.

00:04:37.977 --> 00:04:40.776
You've already met Bramd?

00:04:41.047 --> 00:04:43.744
He gave us a
rather nasty welcome.

00:04:43.816 --> 00:04:48.378
However, that ice dragon
most definitely regrets that now.

00:04:53.459 --> 00:04:57.521
What are you saying?! That dragon
should still be in hibernation!

00:04:57.597 --> 00:05:00.032
And you attacked
and killed him while...!

00:05:00.099 --> 00:05:04.400
A while ago, you released
Bramd from a curse he was under.

00:05:05.405 --> 00:05:09.137
I heard he gave you one of
his treasures as a reward.

00:05:09.208 --> 00:05:14.044
That treasure was sold off to
pay for the upkeep of this temple.

00:05:15.648 --> 00:05:16.945
I see.

00:05:17.016 --> 00:05:21.647
However, a treasure that could be
traded for money is of no use to me.

00:05:21.721 --> 00:05:24.213
| apologize for
this rude meeting of ours.

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:25.921
Who are you?!

00:05:25.992 --> 00:05:29.724
Ashram... The servant of
Emperor Beld of Marmo...

00:05:29.796 --> 00:05:33.391
...the man who fought to
unite this accursed island.

00:05:34.133 --> 00:05:37.262
Now I have a
question for you, Ashram.

00:05:37.837 --> 00:05:41.535
What do you wish to do once you
have the Governor's Treasures?

00:05:42.175 --> 00:05:46.908
To fulfill my late emperor's wishes
is my desire, the meaning of my life!

00:05:46.979 --> 00:05:50.438
And to do that, I must
possess a great treasure...

00:05:50.516 --> 00:05:52.507
The Scepter of Domination!

00:06:03.096 --> 00:06:08.296
The times are about to move again...
Destiny threatens to leave us behind.

00:06:08.768 --> 00:06:12.227
Mistress Neese, who were they?

00:06:12.872 --> 00:06:16.467
Forgive me, but please summon
Leylia back from Zaxon.

00:06:16.542 --> 00:06:19.944
And have her bring her husband
and my granddaughter as well.

00:06:20.012 --> 00:06:22.743
I must once again entrust
those young people...

00:06:22.815 --> 00:06:25.876
...with the fate of all Lodoss!

00:06:36.162 --> 00:06:39.063
C'mon, Orson!
You're holding us up!

00:06:39.132 --> 00:06:40.861
Our enemies won't run away...

00:06:40.933 --> 00:06:43.027
As much as I wish they would.

00:06:43.102 --> 00:06:44.831
Blood shouldn't be
shed uselessly today...

00:06:45.338 --> 00:06:47.432
Helluva thing
for a mercenary to say!

00:06:47.507 --> 00:06:50.841
He sounds like he's scared of
fighting a village full of hayseeds!

00:06:53.546 --> 00:06:59.246
Look, Orson. We're just going to
2axon to collect some overdue taxes.

00:06:59.552 --> 00:07:03.011
| doubt we'll even
have to fight anybody.

00:07:03.456 --> 00:07:06.756
As long as they shut up
and do what they're told!

00:07:06.826 --> 00:07:10.023
You can save the bossiness
for when we're on the job!

00:07:10.096 --> 00:07:12.827
Are we clear on this, Orson?
Duke Raster has promised us...

00:07:12.899 --> 00:07:16.460
...one-quarter of
the tax levy we recover.

00:07:16.936 --> 00:07:19.200
We hardly ever get
sweet deals like this...

00:07:19.272 --> 00:07:21.400
...so I want you to show
a little more enthusiasm!

00:07:24.210 --> 00:07:26.508
And even saying that,
you're still hopeless.

00:07:27.013 --> 00:07:29.607
If he's not up for this,
he'd better drop out while he can.

00:07:29.682 --> 00:07:31.582
He may look like a merc...

00:07:31.651 --> 00:07:33.813
...but a case of cowardice'll
get him out of this business fast!

00:07:35.421 --> 00:07:38.948
You may say that, but you'd
better not make my partner mad.

00:07:39.025 --> 00:07:42.928
When he gets really angry, he won't
distinguish between friend or foe.

00:07:49.335 --> 00:07:52.498
There it is.
Okay, we follow the plan.

00:08:03.583 --> 00:08:07.178
Trouble! Cecil! Cecil!

00:08:07.987 --> 00:08:09.079
What's wrong, Arteen?

00:08:09.155 --> 00:08:12.022
Some people who look like
soldiers are at the village gates!

00:08:12.091 --> 00:08:13.991
They said they wanted to
speak to a representative!

00:08:14.060 --> 00:08:15.494
To speak to Wise Man Slayn?

00:08:15.561 --> 00:08:17.928
Yeah! They said
they were from Alania!

00:08:17.997 --> 00:08:20.728
The king's ordered them to
collect taxes from us!

00:08:20.800 --> 00:08:23.792
What?! All right!
I'll drive them away!

00:08:23.870 --> 00:08:24.598
By yourself?!

00:08:25.705 --> 00:08:27.002
You're right...

00:08:27.073 --> 00:08:29.303
Call HIM in as well,
just to be safe.

00:08:29.942 --> 00:08:30.602
Right!

00:08:31.611 --> 00:08:34.171
What's the holdup?! Where's
the village representative?

00:08:34.247 --> 00:08:37.774
Don't you know it's rude to make
the king's agents wait like this?

00:08:37.850 --> 00:08:40.581
Oh, please. You really expect
to fight us with those weapons?

00:08:40.653 --> 00:08:44.681
How can they be so gutsy with just
one human sorcerer in the village?

00:08:44.757 --> 00:08:47.089
One little human sorcerer...

00:08:47.159 --> 00:08:49.423
Here he comes.

00:08:49.495 --> 00:08:50.155
Oh, Cecil!

00:08:50.830 --> 00:08:52.628
Are you the
village representative?

00:08:52.698 --> 00:08:55.895
Yes! I'll get
right to the point!

00:08:56.168 --> 00:09:00.833
2axon belongs to no kingdom!
We govern ourselves!

00:09:01.307 --> 00:09:05.039
Duke Raster has no right
to make us pay taxes!

00:09:05.645 --> 00:09:08.945
Now, then, if you understand that,
leave this village at once!

00:09:09.015 --> 00:09:11.712
Hmpf! And just what kinda
cheap tricks did you...

00:09:11.784 --> 00:09:14.981
...show these yokels
to win them over?

00:09:15.054 --> 00:09:17.022
You fake sorcerer!

00:09:17.089 --> 00:09:19.990
What?! Are you
trying to insult me?!

00:09:20.059 --> 00:09:23.757
Well, at least he's got enough
brains to see he's being insulted!

00:09:23.829 --> 00:09:26.161
If that's true, then think
this over carefully!

00:09:26.232 --> 00:09:30.226
It'll be no trouble at all for
us to smash this two-bit village!

00:09:30.303 --> 00:09:33.898
Orson, everyone.
Here it comes. Get back!

00:09:35.441 --> 00:09:39.309
"Manna of all creation...
Become the fires of destruction!"

00:09:39.378 --> 00:09:41.142
Shouldn't we back
off a little further?!

00:09:41.213 --> 00:09:43.944
Oh, like it'll reach us!

00:09:52.024 --> 00:09:53.458
It's burning!

00:09:53.526 --> 00:09:55.995
80, he can use fire spells...

00:09:56.062 --> 00:09:59.498
They're not that much trouble
as long as you don't attack head-on.

00:09:59.565 --> 00:10:00.726
Some big magic.

00:10:02.234 --> 00:10:03.133
Well?!

00:10:03.202 --> 00:10:06.365
Huh?! What's the deal?!
He's a real sorcerer!

00:10:06.439 --> 00:10:08.305
They didn't say anything about
this! Run for it, Orson!

00:10:08.374 --> 00:10:11.173
Hah! You won't get away!

00:10:14.647 --> 00:10:17.082
Where did they go?

00:10:17.249 --> 00:10:19.183
Damn! It's a trap!

00:10:19.251 --> 00:10:23.779
Yeah, and I didn't think you'd
fall for one this simple, either.

00:10:24.824 --> 00:10:28.317
You can't hit all of us with
one magic spell at this range.

00:10:30.062 --> 00:10:34.431
Anyway, why don't you drop
that sorcerer's staff, Slayn?

00:10:35.234 --> 00:10:36.929
What's wrong? Hurry up!

00:10:37.003 --> 00:10:39.904
| see... My name is Cecil.

00:10:40.740 --> 00:10:43.937
I'm the captain of Slayn's
self-defense force while he's away.

00:10:44.010 --> 00:10:47.002
What? They have
TWO sorcerers?

00:10:47.079 --> 00:10:49.241
Duke Raster said
there was only one.

00:10:50.383 --> 00:10:55.116
Whoever you are, it doesn't change
the fact that you're now our hostage!

00:10:55.187 --> 00:10:58.122
Even if you take me hostage...

00:10:58.190 --> 00:11:00.682
...2axon won't pay these taxes
for you to keep waging wars!

00:11:01.193 --> 00:11:02.854
If you're going to
kill me, then kill me!

00:11:02.928 --> 00:11:05.920
You've got a lot of guts.
Fine, as you wish!

00:11:05.998 --> 00:11:08.126
Is it necessary
to kill him?

00:11:08.200 --> 00:11:12.467
Like I care?! If we get made fools
of on a job, that's it for us!

00:11:16.042 --> 00:11:19.535
Come on! If you're gonna cry
or beg for mercy, now's the time!

00:11:26.986 --> 00:11:31.389
You're being protected by the
sylph. You're safe now, Cecil.

00:11:31.924 --> 00:11:32.755
That voice...!

00:11:33.592 --> 00:11:34.582
Shoot!

00:11:37.496 --> 00:11:38.986
What?!

00:11:39.065 --> 00:11:42.501
Wind spirits?! But he didn't
cast a spell, did he?

00:11:42.568 --> 00:11:45.765
It wasn't his doing.
It's an elf.

00:11:45.838 --> 00:11:47.863
An elf?!

00:11:54.246 --> 00:11:57.011
Cecil, really! You can be
so careless sometimes!

00:11:57.483 --> 00:11:59.008
Deed!

00:11:59.085 --> 00:12:01.577
Cecil!
I'll take it from here!

00:12:03.856 --> 00:12:04.982
Parn!

00:12:05.057 --> 00:12:08.823
You people! Stop this at once,
or else I'll show you no mercy!

00:12:09.428 --> 00:12:14.127
Parn! I've heard of you... The
swordsman who travels with an elf.

00:12:14.734 --> 00:12:17.328
The famous free knight, Parn!

00:12:17.403 --> 00:12:19.201
Facing him alone
will be dangerous.

00:12:19.271 --> 00:12:21.035
Stay out of this, Orson.

00:12:21.440 --> 00:12:25.468
Interesting! I've wanted
to get a shot at fighting you!

00:12:25.544 --> 00:12:29.208
Keep those other two out of this
so they can't help him with magic!

00:12:51.036 --> 00:12:54.563
"Gentle atmosphere
which brings sleep..."

00:12:55.541 --> 00:12:57.566
"Sylph of the
free-blowing winds."

00:12:57.643 --> 00:13:01.477
"Let the trembling of the air
cease, let all sounds vanish..."

00:13:10.689 --> 00:13:11.349
Deed!

00:13:12.591 --> 00:13:16.960
"Manna of all creation...
Become the fires of destruction!"

00:13:20.366 --> 00:13:22.425
What did you do to him?

00:13:22.501 --> 00:13:25.903
| cast a spell of silence
to try to confuse him.

00:13:25.971 --> 00:13:28.565
But, even when all
sound suddenly vanished...

00:13:28.641 --> 00:13:31.372
...he didn't seem
disturbed by it at all.

00:13:37.249 --> 00:13:39.980
Drop the sword.
You can't beat me.

00:13:41.020 --> 00:13:42.419
SHUT UP!

00:13:48.027 --> 00:13:50.962
He's coming
this way! Deed!

00:14:02.575 --> 00:14:04.634
Shirts...

00:14:25.564 --> 00:14:29.660
Oh, well. I accept that
you've beaten me, Mr. Warrior.

00:14:29.735 --> 00:14:31.726
Will you listen to me now?

00:14:31.804 --> 00:14:35.035
Of course. Since you beat me,
I have to do what you say.

00:14:40.279 --> 00:14:43.271
However, you have
to let me live.

00:14:43.349 --> 00:14:46.478
That's not much of a
condition in a surrender.

00:14:48.721 --> 00:14:50.712
Orson?!

00:15:03.302 --> 00:15:05.396
Quick! Drop your sword!
Orson's...!

00:15:06.338 --> 00:15:08.204
Parn, run!

00:15:08.274 --> 00:15:10.174
PARN!

00:15:26.325 --> 00:15:29.386
Stop it, Orson!
I'm all right!

00:15:30.896 --> 00:15:33.957
Orson!
Don't you understand me?!

00:15:34.033 --> 00:15:35.831
| thought there
was something strange.

00:15:35.901 --> 00:15:39.769
Nothing will affect him now...
He's a berserker!

00:15:40.172 --> 00:15:41.640
A berserker?!

00:15:41.707 --> 00:15:45.769
That man is controlled by
the spirit of rage and anger.

00:15:45.844 --> 00:15:49.906
The only feelings in his heart now
are of anger and the need to kill!

00:15:49.982 --> 00:15:51.313
What did you say?!

00:15:51.383 --> 00:15:55.149
People who become berserkers can't
distinguish between friend or foe.

00:15:55.220 --> 00:15:58.019
They keep on killing and killing until
their body literally falls apart.

00:15:58.090 --> 00:16:01.890
You've gotta be kidding! Zaxon
village is right in front of him!

00:16:01.961 --> 00:16:03.395
If a guy like
that gets in there...!

00:16:03.462 --> 00:16:05.362
Parn!

00:16:12.604 --> 00:16:14.868
Orson, stop it!

00:16:15.574 --> 00:16:17.736
Stop it, Orson!

00:16:24.650 --> 00:16:25.515
Orson!

00:16:28.554 --> 00:16:30.488
Orson!

00:16:34.259 --> 00:16:36.887
| see. So, this is
a herserker, huh?

00:16:36.962 --> 00:16:37.952
You!

00:16:38.030 --> 00:16:40.590
What are you doing?!
Use this chance to escape!

00:16:40.666 --> 00:16:43.158
Wh- Who said
I needed to be saved?!

00:16:48.440 --> 00:16:50.431
He's so strong...!

00:17:07.559 --> 00:17:10.529
Deed! It doesn't look like
| can beat him with just a sword!

00:17:10.596 --> 00:17:12.587
It looks that way.

00:17:13.832 --> 00:17:17.735
"Gentle spirits of the forest...
Please, give me your strength!”

00:17:22.908 --> 00:17:25.468
"Leprechauns,
spirits of confusion.”

00:17:25.544 --> 00:17:28.104
"Shades, controllers of fear."

00:17:28.180 --> 00:17:32.117
"Disrupt just a bit the
anger which controls him!"

00:17:40.125 --> 00:17:42.560
It looks like it's
working. Okay, Deed!

00:17:42.628 --> 00:17:46.531
"Spirits of enchantment, spirits
of chaos, spirits of darkness..."

00:17:46.598 --> 00:17:50.034
Orson! Can you hear my
voice?! Wake up, Orson!

00:17:57.443 --> 00:17:58.638
Parn, finish him!

00:17:58.710 --> 00:18:00.178
Gotcha!

00:18:00.245 --> 00:18:02.270
Wait! Don't kill him!

00:18:02.347 --> 00:18:03.678
Move aside!

00:18:03.749 --> 00:18:07.344
No, I won't!
He isn't a berserker anymore!

00:18:07.853 --> 00:18:09.480
He's back to normal!

00:18:09.555 --> 00:18:10.454
Move!

00:18:10.522 --> 00:18:13.287
| won't move! I can't stand
by and let my friend be killed!

00:18:18.931 --> 00:18:21.992
Let your friend be killed, huh?

00:18:22.201 --> 00:18:26.502
We'll patch up your wounds. You can
tell us the details in the village.

00:18:26.572 --> 00:18:28.165
Orson!

00:18:28.240 --> 00:18:30.902
Orson, snap out of it.

00:18:34.413 --> 00:18:37.383
A long time ago, Orson saw
his real older sister...

00:18:37.449 --> 00:18:39.474
...get killed right
before his eyes.

00:18:40.352 --> 00:18:43.617
Since then, whenever he sees
a girl who looks like...

00:18:43.689 --> 00:18:46.590
...she's about to be killed, he
starts fighting like a madman.

00:18:46.658 --> 00:18:49.491
You could say that
what's done is done...

00:18:49.561 --> 00:18:52.326
...but if that war hadn't
happened back then...

00:18:52.397 --> 00:18:56.197
...then maybe Orson wouldn't
be the way he is today.

00:18:56.935 --> 00:18:59.768
The War of Heroes may have
ended, but it seems...

00:18:59.838 --> 00:19:03.638
...there are still places in Lodoss
where its wounds haven't healed.

00:19:03.709 --> 00:19:06.906
By the way, what are
you going to do to us?

00:19:06.979 --> 00:19:11.416
If you swear you'll never come to
this village again, I'll let you go.

00:19:11.483 --> 00:19:14.145
And take your violent
fighter friend with you.

00:19:14.219 --> 00:19:17.211
Oh, my.
Everyone's here already!

00:19:17.289 --> 00:19:19.121
Master Slayn!

00:19:19.191 --> 00:19:20.818
Welcome home!

00:19:20.893 --> 00:19:23.225
What in the world happened here?

00:19:23.295 --> 00:19:25.730
Parn, you look a little worn out.

00:19:25.797 --> 00:19:29.631
Of course. As usual, I was
risking my life to save the village.

00:19:29.701 --> 00:19:31.169
It wears me out.

00:19:32.371 --> 00:19:34.601
You don't usually take Leylia and...

00:19:34.673 --> 00:19:36.869
Little Neese with you
when you leave.

00:19:36.942 --> 00:19:39.377
Little Neese,
where did you all go?

00:19:41.313 --> 00:19:43.714
To see Grandma Big Neese!

00:19:44.116 --> 00:19:46.847
You went to see Mistress Neese
at the temple of Marfa?

00:19:46.919 --> 00:19:51.755
Yes, that's right. I received
an urgent message from Mother.

00:19:52.324 --> 00:19:53.291
It's for Parn as well.

00:19:53.358 --> 00:19:57.226
Give me a break for today.
Save it for tomorrow.

00:19:57.396 --> 00:19:59.956
Then I'll fight the dragon
or whatever it is.

00:20:00.032 --> 00:20:02.865
Really? You're a lifesaver.

00:20:02.935 --> 00:20:07.600
| was really worried about
getting you to fight a dragon...

00:20:08.574 --> 00:20:11.373
...but you've saved me
from having to convince you.

00:20:11.443 --> 00:20:13.969
Fight a dragon...?!

00:20:14.079 --> 00:20:17.674
Yes. For the sake of Lodoss!
At any cost!

00:20:22.788 --> 00:20:23.949
Welcome...

00:20:24.022 --> 00:20:25.581
...to Lodoss Island!

00:20:25.657 --> 00:20:27.022
And now, what you've
all been waiting for...

00:20:27.092 --> 00:20:28.856
The second part of the show!

00:20:33.031 --> 00:20:34.692
To the south of the
continent of Alecrast...

00:20:34.766 --> 00:20:37.098
...lies the accursed
island of Lodoss.

00:20:38.237 --> 00:20:41.764
It's covered by all sorts of
kingdoms, both large and small.

00:20:44.009 --> 00:20:49.345
Parn is a free knight, meaning
he isn't bound by any one kingdom.

00:20:49.414 --> 00:20:50.779
Right, Parn?

00:20:50.849 --> 00:20:54.615
If he swears loyalty to one
kingdom, he can't help any others.

00:20:54.686 --> 00:20:55.676
As a free knight,

00:20:55.754 --> 00:20:58.780
you want to help all people
who live on Lodoss, right?!

00:21:02.127 --> 00:21:05.927
Oh, Parn! Once you set
your mind on something...

00:21:05.998 --> 00:21:09.332
...you really don't notice
anything else, do you?

00:21:09.401 --> 00:21:12.962
But, that's what it is about
Parn that makes me, er, um...

00:21:13.038 --> 00:21:15.200
LOVE HIm!

00:21:17.075 --> 00:21:19.305
Lo-0-0-ove him!

00:21:19.911 --> 00:21:21.606
Slayn...!

00:21:21.680 --> 00:21:25.776
What's wrong, Deed? Why'd
the spirit of anger appear?

00:21:26.084 --> 00:21:29.611
Uh, k- keep fighting to build
that wonderful tomorrow, Parn!

00:21:29.688 --> 00:21:32.817
Don't give up, Parn!
We're the heroes!

00:21:33.458 --> 00:21:35.256
Pow-pow, Parn!

00:21:35.327 --> 00:21:36.988
C'mon, join in!

00:21:37.062 --> 00:21:39.963
Pow-pow, Parn!
Pow-pow, Parn!

00:21:40.532 --> 00:21:43.263
Now go, Free Knight of Lodoss!

00:21:43.335 --> 00:21:46.828
So, he's the infamous free
knight I've heard about.

00:21:46.905 --> 00:21:47.599
Go!

00:21:47.673 --> 00:21:49.141
Pow-pow, Parn!

00:21:49.207 --> 00:21:54.043
| want you to fight a terrible
dragon for the sake of Lodoss!

00:21:54.112 --> 00:21:57.446
He's tough!
Be strong, brave knight!

00:21:57.549 --> 00:21:58.914
Pow-pow, Parn!

00:21:58.984 --> 00:21:59.644
Huh?

00:21:59.718 --> 00:22:04.781
Pow-pow, Parn! Pow-pow, Parn!
Pow-pow, Parn! Pow-pow, Parn!

00:22:06.091 --> 00:22:07.286
Parn, you, too!

00:22:07.359 --> 00:22:08.690
Me?

00:22:09.861 --> 00:22:11.590
But what exactly
does any of this mean?

00:22:11.963 --> 00:22:14.091
That you never know
what'll happen next.

00:22:14.166 --> 00:22:17.101
Welcome to Lodoss Island!
Pleased to meet you all!

00:23:38.917 --> 00:23:42.012
A sudden mission
to become dragon slayers.

00:23:42.087 --> 00:23:45.079
That's what Neese, the Priestess
of the earth goddess Marfa...

00:23:45.157 --> 00:23:46.784
...has charged Slayn with.

00:23:46.858 --> 00:23:51.295
Now is the time to reveal
the dark memory kept for 500 years.

00:23:52.063 --> 00:23:55.829
Next time, on Record of Lodoss Wars -
Chronicles of the Heroic Knight:

00:23:55.901 --> 00:23:58.461
"Dragon... The Guardian
of the Lost History".
